  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return grid\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Create output grid as copy\n    output = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # Extract signature from top row (row 0)\n    signature = []\n    for c in range(cols):\n        if grid[0][c] != 0:\n            signature.append((c, grid[0][c]))\n    \n    # Clear top row\n    for c in range(cols):\n        output[0][c] = 0\n    \n    # Find the shape color (most common non-zero color excluding row 0 and col 0)\n    from collections import Counter\n    color_count = Counter()\n    for r in range(1, rows):\n        for c in range(1, cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                color_count[grid[r][c]] += 1\n    \n    if not color_count:\n        return output\n    \n    shape_color = color_count.most_common(1)[0][0]\n    \n    # Process each row with a marker in column 0\n    for r in range(1, rows):\n        marker = grid[r][0]\n        if marker == 0:\n            continue\n        \n        # Clear the marker\n        output[r][0] = 0\n        \n        # Find extent of shape in this row\n        leftmost = None\n        rightmost = None\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == shape_color:\n                if leftmost is None:\n                    leftmost = c\n                rightmost = c\n        \n        if leftmost is None:\n            continue\n        \n        # Determine start position based on marker\n        sig_values = [v for _, v in signature]\n        if not sig_values:\n            continue\n            \n        if marker == 3:\n            # Align to left with offset -1\n            start_col = leftmost - 1\n        else:  # marker == 2 or others\n            # Align to right with offset +1 (ending at rightmost + 1)\n            start_col = rightmost + 1 - len(sig_values)\n        \n        # Place signature values\n        for i, val in enumerate(sig_values):\n            c = start_col + i\n            if 0 <= c < cols:\n                output[r][c] = val\n    \n    return output\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return grid\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Create output grid as copy\n    output = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # Extract signature from top row (row 0)\n    signature = []\n    for c in range(cols):\n        if grid[0][c] != 0:\n            signature.append((c, grid[0][c]))\n    \n    # Clear top row\n    for c in range(cols):\n        output[0][c] = 0\n    \n    # Find the shape color (most common non-zero color excluding row 0 and col 0)\n    from collections import Counter\n    color_count = Counter()\n    for r in range(1, rows):\n        for c in range(1, cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                color_count[grid[r][c]] += 1\n    \n    if not color_count:\n        return output\n    \n    shape_color = color_count.most_common(1)[0][0]\n    \n    # Process each row with a marker in column 0\n    for r in range(1, rows):\n        marker = grid[r][0]\n        if marker == 0:\n            continue\n        \n        # Clear the marker\n        output[r][0] = 0\n        \n        # Find extent of shape in this row\n        leftmost = None\n        rightmost = None\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == shape_color:\n                if leftmost is None:\n                    leftmost = c\n                rightmost = c\n        \n        if leftmost is None:\n            continue\n        \n        # Determine start position based on marker\n        sig_values = [v for _, v in signature]\n        if not sig_values:\n            continue\n            \n        if marker == 3:\n            # Align to left with offset -1\n            start_col = leftmost - 1\n        else:  # marker == 2 or others\n            # Align to right with offset +1 (ending at rightmost + 1)\n            start_col = rightmost + 1 - len(sig_values)\n        \n        # Place signature values\n        for i, val in enumerate(sig_values):\n         